      "abstract": "<jats:p>Let α be an arbitrary positive number. For every integer <jats:italic>n</jats:italic> ≦ 0 we can write<jats:disp-formula><jats:graphic xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" mime-subtype=\"gif\" mimetype=\"image\" position=\"float\" xlink:type=\"simple\" xlink:href=\"S1446788700005371_eqn1\"/></jats:disp-formula> where <jats:disp-formula><jats:graphic xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" mime-subtype=\"gif\" mimetype=\"image\" position=\"float\" xlink:type=\"simple\" xlink:href=\"S1446788700005371_eqn2\"/></jats:disp-formula> is the largest integer not greater than<jats:inline-graphic xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" mime-subtype=\"gif\" mimetype=\"image\" xlink:type=\"simple\" xlink:href=\"S1446788700005371_inline1\"/>, i.e the integral part of<jats:inline-graphic xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" mime-subtype=\"gif\" mimetype=\"image\" xlink:type=\"simple\" xlink:href=\"S1446788700005371_inline1\"/>, and <jats:italic>r<jats:sub>n</jats:sub></jats:italic> is its fractional part and so satisfies the inequality<jats:disp-formula><jats:graphic xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" mime-subtype=\"gif\" mimetype=\"image\" position=\"float\" xlink:type=\"simple\" xlink:href=\"S1446788700005371_eqn3\"/></jats:disp-formula></jats:p>",
